-- title:
--   Node depth along the degeneracy tower is a ramification power
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime not dividing $N\ge 1$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose nonunits contain the image of $q$, so that $k:=$ `ResidueField A` has characteristic $q$. Fix: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$ whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q N k` (rational places at which $j$ and $j_N$ are both regular and whose $j$-value is supersingular); modular polynomial data `data` at $q$ whose $\Phi$ reduces mod $q$ to $(Y^{q}-X)(Y-X^{q})$; integrality of the level-$q$ degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` at level $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a place specialisation $P$ of the level-$Nq$ situation at $A$ with residue map `residue A`; a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$ satisfying `IsModel`, `OrderLawFixed`, and the regularity and node-value laws on $W$; and, for each $w\in W$, a finite extension $K_w$ of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, node coordinates $(x_w,y_w)$ in the node ring over $K_w$ at $w$ (each vanishing on one branch and of order one on the other), an element $\varpi_w$ of $A\cap K_w$ generating the kernel of `redRestrict`, the value-integrality law at $w$, and an identity $x_w y_w = \mathrm{nodeConst}(\varpi_w)^{E}u$ with $E\ge 1$ and $u$ a unit. Assume the same package at level $N\ell$ for a prime $\ell\neq q$, yielding $W_r$, $P_r$, $R_r$, $K_{r,\bullet}$, node coordinates, uniformisers and crossing identities (hypotheses summarised here). Assume moreover that `towerInclBar` for $Nq\mid N\ell q$ is integral, that `heckeAlphaC k N ℓ` (the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` into the roof `charLDegeneracyRoof k N ℓ`, the subfield generated by $j$, $j_N$, $j_\ell$, $j_{N\ell}$) is integral, and that `modularFunctionFieldC k (N*ℓ)` lies in the roof by an integral inclusion. Then for every place $y_1$ of the roof, every $y\in W_r$ and $w\in W$ such that $y_1$ restricts to $y$ along the roof inclusion and to $w$ along `heckeAlphaC`, and every place $V'$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N*ℓ*q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P_r.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V'=y$ and $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}$ of the restriction of $V'$ along `towerInclBar` equal to $w$: the depth of that restriction at $w$, namely the $A$-valuation of the value of $y_w$ at it, equals the $A$-valuation of the value of $y_{r,y}$ at $V'$ raised to the power `ramificationIndexAlong` of $y_1$ over `heckeAlphaC`; and the restriction of $V'$ is strict for $P$ (its first reduction is carried to its second by geometric Frobenius, and is not fixed by the square of that Frobenius) if and only if $V'$ is strict for $P_r$.
--
--   This is the comparison, at a supersingular node, of the local crossing parameter between level $N$ and level $N\ell$ along the forgetful degeneracy leg for a prime $\ell$ different from the residue characteristic: depths multiply as ramification indices in the tower, and the strictness of a place over the node is preserved. It feeds the level-$N\ell$ form of the depth formula along `heckeAlphaBar`.
